Short: Finds File-descriptions from BBS-list
Uploader: Michael Gehmair <mike_sp@sbox.tu-graz.ac.at>
Author: Michael Gehmair <mike_sp@sbox.tu-graz.ac.at>
Type: comm/bbs

IDFind is for all who are used to extract the File_ID.Diz File
for making a list. As a matter of fact sometimes File_ID.Diz is not found.
To complete your list you have to get the Upload-file from your local BBS
and search for the file.

Here is where IDFind drops in. Just give the BBSList and the NoFileIDList and
IDFind finds the Description for you and writes them into a 3rd File.
If for some reason some files are not in the BBSList, they will be stored
into a 4th File. You can create the NoFileIDList by simply by recording
a Macro in you favourite Editor where you search for the NoFile_id.diz 
string and copy it to a new file. The output should look like the
NoFileIDList in the IDFile Directory.

For Demonstration purpose i included a short BBSfile and a NoFileIDList.
Start with:

   IDFind NoFileIDList BBSList FoundList NotFound

where FoundList is the list where the found descriptions are stored and
NotFound is the list of the file were no Description was available in BBSList

Note: IDFind is intended for excessive BBS-Users. Others may not find very
      much use for it.

